WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.500
This is Allen Company task training for mechanics,

00:07.500 --> 00:10.250
welders and anyone working in the shop.

00:10.250 --> 00:13.100
The shop has every kind of hazard in one building:

00:13.100 --> 00:16.550
stored energy, heavy parts, heat, chemicals and

00:16.550 --> 00:17.413
fire.

00:18.540 --> 00:21.378
At Boonesboro, the mine shop is underground,

00:21.378 --> 00:24.477
on Level 1. Equipment moves in and out of the bay

00:24.477 --> 00:28.053
all day, so watch for it. Certain shop tasks,

00:28.053 --> 00:30.928
like some welding, grinding and cleaning jobs,

00:30.928 --> 00:33.403
need a respirator. Your supervisor will tell you

00:33.403 --> 00:34.190
which.

00:37.510 --> 00:39.735
Repairs and maintenance are done with the power

00:39.735 --> 00:42.973
off and the machine blocked against hazardous motion.

00:42.973 --> 00:45.673
Pull the key, lock it out, disconnect the battery

00:45.673 --> 00:49.135
where needed, chock the wheels, and bleed off hydraulic

00:49.135 --> 00:52.248
and air pressure. Only where testing requires power

00:52.248 --> 00:55.148
is it done with power on, and then only with extra

00:55.148 --> 00:56.285
precautions.

00:57.400 --> 00:59.813
Never work under a raised dump body,

00:59.813 --> 01:02.763
bucket or machine held up only by hydraulics or

01:02.763 --> 01:06.000
a jack. Use the body prop, cylinder lock,

01:06.000 --> 01:08.788
jack stands or cribbing rated for the load.

01:09.898 --> 01:11.998
On electrical equipment and circuits,

01:11.998 --> 01:14.986
the power is off, locked and tagged by the person

01:14.986 --> 01:17.861
doing the work, and tested before you touch it.

01:17.861 --> 01:20.473
Only qualified people do electrical work.

01:23.804 --> 01:26.329
Large tires hold enough energy to kill.

01:26.329 --> 01:29.029
Before a tire comes off, deflate it by removing

01:29.029 --> 01:32.654
the valve core. Inflate multi-piece or large rims

01:32.654 --> 01:35.879
in a cage or restraint, with a clip-on chuck and

01:35.879 --> 01:38.579
a remote gauge, standing out of the trajectory

01:38.579 --> 01:41.967
path. Never weld or heat on a rim with the tire

01:41.967 --> 01:42.779
mounted.

01:46.123 --> 01:48.323
Wear the protective clothing and eye protection

01:48.323 --> 01:51.723
for welding, cutting and grinding. A face shield

01:51.723 --> 01:53.760
or goggles when you're using a grinder.

01:54.901 --> 01:57.788
Before hot work, move or cover anything that can

01:57.788 --> 02:00.401
burn, and keep an extinguisher right there.

02:00.401 --> 02:03.838
Never weld or cut on tanks or lines that held fuel

02:03.838 --> 02:06.838
or oil until they've been cleaned. At Allen,

02:06.838 --> 02:09.251
hot work needs a written hot-work permit,

02:09.251 --> 02:11.776
and after you finish, someone keeps a fire watch

02:11.776 --> 02:13.713
on the area for 30 minutes.

02:17.026 --> 02:19.714
Check slings and hooks before every lift,

02:19.714 --> 02:22.826
never exceed the rated capacity, and never stand

02:22.826 --> 02:26.301
or walk under a suspended load. Use a tag line.

02:27.412 --> 02:30.125
Clean up spills right away, keep aisles clear and

02:30.125 --> 02:33.300
put tools back. Slips and trips are the most common

02:33.300 --> 02:34.562
shop injuries.

02:37.886 --> 02:40.923
Recap: power off, locked and blocked.

02:40.923 --> 02:43.573
Never under raised equipment held by hydraulics

02:43.573 --> 02:47.149
or jacks. Deflate before removing tires and inflate

02:47.149 --> 02:50.236
in a cage. Wear the right PPE for hot work and

02:50.236 --> 02:53.586
clear combustibles. Respect the crane's capacity.

02:53.586 --> 02:56.149
Keep it clean. Chemicals in the shop are covered

02:56.149 --> 02:57.686
in the HazCom lesson.

02:58.808 --> 03:01.970
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:01.970 --> 03:03.471
override this video.
